          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pratīkṣate is built on prati, \"towards\", and the root √īkṣ, \"to look\" (MW): to wait is to look out for someone. It means \"beholds\" in the Atharvaveda and \"waits for\" in the Taittirīya Saṃhitā (CDIAL 8620); Marathi paikhṇẽ means \"to wait for\"."
            }
          ]
